### Goal Model Decomposition

---

#### **Goal Tables**

| Goal ID | Goal Title                 | Text                                                                 | Runtime Annotation | Goal Type | Relation | Justification |
|---------|----------------------------|----------------------------------------------------------------------|--------------------|-----------|----------|----------------|
| G1      | Fulfill Resource Request   | Ensure the requested resources are collected and delivered to the destination. | -                  | Achieve   | -        | Primary mission objective: collect and deliver resources. |
| G2      | Collect Resources from Storage | Retrieve required resources from storage locations in an optimized order. | ;                  | Perform   | G1       | Collection must precede delivery (AND). |
| G3      | Deliver Resources to Requesting Agent | Transport collected resources to the specified destination. | ;                  | Perform   | G1       | Delivery must follow collection (AND). |
| G2.1    | Determine Storage Order    | Calculate the optimal order of storage visits based on waiting time and path. | -                  | Query     | G2       | Required to optimize resource retrieval. |
| G2.2    | Collect Resources from Each Storage | Retrieve resources from each storage in the determined order. | #                  | Perform   | G2       | Parallel execution allows multiple robots to handle different storages. |
| G3.1    | Determine Delivery Route   | Plan the route for transporting resources to the destination. | -                  | Query     | G3       | Required to optimize delivery path. |
| G3.2    | Deliver Resources in Batches | Transport resources in batches to the destination as needed. | ;                  | Perform   | G3       | Sequential execution ensures all resources are delivered. |
| G4      | Handle Low Battery During Collection | Return to recharging station if battery drops below 10% during collection. | FALLBACK(G2.2, G4.1) | Perform   | G2.2     | Fallback for low battery during collection. |
| G4.1    | Recharge and Reassign Task | Return to recharging station and assign remaining task to another robot. | -                  | Perform   | G4       | Mandatory fallback action when battery is critically low. |
| G5      | Handle Low Battery During Delivery | Return to checkpoint if battery drops below 30% during delivery. | FALLBACK(G3.2, G5.1) | Perform   | G3.2     | Fallback for low battery during delivery. |
| G5.1    | Return to Checkpoint and Reassign | Return resources to a checkpoint and assign remaining task to another robot. | -                  | Perform   | G5       | Mandatory fallback action when battery is low during delivery. |

